      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so when you say it \"fundamentally undermines the separation of powers,\" are you saying that the dissent's entire logic is basically just an attempt to bypass the legislative process through the court? i'm trying to pin down if their position is actually a legitimate legal theory that scholars debate, or if it's just widely seen in the legal community as a way to implement policy through judicial fiat?",
